      "title": "SB 3125 CD1 and Announcement 2024-03, read 28 Nov 2026",
      "note": "New 2027 tables (single): 1.4% to $14,400, 2.5% to $19,200, 5% to $24,000, 6.4% to $36,000, 6.8% to $48,000, 7.2% to $125,000, 7.6% to $175,000, 8.25% to $225,000, 9% to $275,000, 10% to $325,000, 11% to $500,000, 13% above; joint doubles the thresholds to $1,000,000. Section 9: Part I applies to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2026. The statute's tables use rounded base amounts (e.g. $202.00 for 1.4% of $14,400), so a bracket calculation can differ from the official table by under $1."
